# Pass Models, Const Constructors, Own Files

## Pass the Model, Not Primitives

When a widget needs multiple fields from one data model, pass the whole object. Do not destructure into primitive constructor params.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
class AnimalTile extends StatelessWidget {
  const AnimalTile({
    super.key,
    required this.name,
    required this.species,
    required this.age,
  });
  final String name;
  final String species;
  final int age;
}

// ✅ GOOD
class AnimalTile extends StatelessWidget {
  const AnimalTile({super.key, required this.animal});
  final Animal animal;
}
```

Primitive or simple params are fine when the widget truly needs only one value (e.g. a title `String`, a flag `bool`).

## Prefer const constructors

Every `StatelessWidget` / immutable widget should expose a `const` constructor when all fields are immutable. Use `const` at call sites when possible.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
class AnimalHeader extends StatelessWidget {
  AnimalHeader({super.key, required this.title});
  final String title;
}

// ✅ GOOD
class AnimalHeader extends StatelessWidget {
  const AnimalHeader({super.key, required this.title});
  final String title;
}
```

## One widget per file

Put each custom widget in its own file under a nearby `widgets/` folder. Do not nest multiple widget classes in a screen file.

```dart
// ❌ BAD — AnimalListPage and AnimalTile in the same file

// ✅ GOOD
// animal_list_page.dart → AnimalListPage only
// widgets/animal_tile.dart → AnimalTile only
```
